      "ae.faq": [{"q": "What do I do if the pack crashes?", "a": "The most common cause is not enough <b>RAM</b> or the wrong Java version. Allocate 6–8 GB and pick <b>Java 17</b>. Run <code>crash-report.txt</code> through the \"Techno-Doctor\" in Tech Bay — it’ll point straight to the cause."}, {"q": "How much RAM should I allocate?", "a": "<b>8 GB</b> is optimal, 6 is the minimum. More than 10–12 GB gives no benefit. The <b>RAM Calculator</b> in Tech Bay will give you the exact argument string."}, {"q": "How do I enable shaders?", "a": "<b>Options → Video Settings → Shader Packs</b>, pick a profile (Potato → Extreme) for your hardware. Everything is already tuned for the cold atmosphere."}, {"q": "Why are some blocks purple?", "a": "That’s a known texture bug in a couple of mods (e.g. <code>create_bic_bit</code>). It <b>doesn’t affect stability</b> — waiting on the authors to update."}, {"q": "Can I play without shaders?", "a": "Yes, the pack is fully playable with vanilla lighting. FPS is higher without shaders, the mechanics stay identical."}, {"q": "Where do I suggest ideas or report bugs?", "a": "Right here, in the \"Bonfire\": the <b>\"Suggestions & Ideas\"</b> and <b>\"Tech Support\"</b> tabs. The best ideas rise with upvotes."}],
