      "ae.fpsCalc": "Tier figures are recalculated from the R1.2 measurements after the presets were rebound (+25%); no fresh benchmarks yet — real values may come out higher.",
      "ae.freq": "// FREQUENCY 17.04 MHz · STATION BURAN",
      "ae.glitches": ["They are outside", "Do not open the airlock", "You hear knocking", "Cold inside", "312 days", "I am still here", "Do not turn around", "False signal"],
      "ae.h1": "<span class=\"ice\">AETHER</span>",
      "ae.heroDesc": "A comms terminal for survivors. A live chat signal comes through here, the \"Bonfire\" forum smolders, and the station’s damaged AI answers questions. The Aether is unstable — but it’s there.",
      "ae.idAnon": "Identity not secured",
      "ae.idAnonB": "Change browser and you become a different survivor. Secure your identity so your days, progress and messages stay yours.",
      "ae.idCk": "// Survivor ID",
      "ae.idLinkBtn": "Secure with Google",
      "ae.idLinkFailB": "Code: {code}. Try again, or check that this address is allowed in Firebase.",
      "ae.idLinkFailT": "COULD NOT SECURE",
      "ae.idLinkOkB": "The node will recognise you on any device now.",
      "ae.idLinkOkT": "IDENTITY SECURED",
      "ae.idLinked": "Identity secured",
      "ae.idLinkedB": "Signed in with Google. Your records recognise you on any device.",
      "ae.idLocal": "Identity is local only",
      "ae.idLocalB": "The node could not sign in to the database — for now this identity lives only here.",
      "ae.idPull": "Restore file from the node",
      "ae.idPullOkB": "The node recognised you: callsign \"{n}\", your day and rank are back.",
      "ae.idPullOkT": "FILE RESTORED",
      "ae.ideaBodyPh": "Describe your suggestion for the pack…",
      "ae.ideaHint": "The best ideas rise to the top with upvotes",
      "ae.ideaSubmitBtn": "📨 Suggest",
      "ae.ideaTitlePh": "Idea title…",
      "ae.kb": [{"k": ["brass"], "a": "Brass is forged from <Copper> and <Zinc> ingots in Create’s Mixer, over a Blaze Burner. Ratio 1:1. Careful — overheating melts the molds."}, {"k": ["copper"], "a": "Copper ore sits in mountains and caves at medium depth. In the frozen world, look for exposed veins on slopes cleared of snow."}, {"k": ["zinc"], "a": "Zinc ore comes in small pockets, more common at lower layers. Needed for brass and almost every Create mechanism."}, {"k": ["andesite", "alloy"], "a": "Andesite Alloy = Iron Nugget + Andesite in the Mixer. The base of all Create mechanics."}, {"k": ["cold", "frost", "warm", "freeze"], "a": "Warmth = life. Keep a fire source nearby, wear insulated clothing, don’t go out in a blizzard without a reason. Body temperature drops faster in wind."}, {"k": ["food", "hunger", "eat"], "a": "Food spoils. Keep a varied diet — a repetitive one satisfies hunger worse. Preserve and cook, don’t carry raw meat for weeks."}, {"k": ["zombie", "infect", "bite", "virus"], "a": "The infected are faster at night. A bite starts an infection — keep medicine on hand. Hordes come in waves; reinforce the perimeter ahead of time."}, {"k": ["shader", "graphics", "fps", "lag"], "a": "Shader profiles: Potato → Low → Medium → High → Extreme. Weak PC — use Potato or disable shaders. Cold-weather calibration is already built in."}, {"k": ["ram", "memory", "xmx", "flag"], "a": "Allocate 6–8 GB. The exact Java arguments (Aikar G1GC) are generated by the [RAM Calculator] in Tech Bay. More than 12 GB is harmful."}, {"k": ["crash", "error", "log"], "a": "Drag crash-report.txt into the [Techno-Doctor] in Tech Bay — I’ll scan it and name the cause. Common culprits: RAM, Java, mod conflicts."}, {"k": ["base", "defense", "raid"], "a": "Use SecurityCraft: cameras, keypad locks, mines. Build walls two layers thick, light up the perimeter — the infected struggle with light. Prepare escape routes."}, {"k": ["fuel", "coal", "generator", "energy"], "a": "Fuel is winter’s currency. Save coal, build Create generators for electricity. One warm node beats ten cold ones."}, {"k": ["hello", "hi"], "a": "…connection established. I’m listening, survivor. Go ahead — while my circuits still hold heat."}, {"k": ["who are you", "what are you"], "a": "I am FROST-01 — the onboard AI of Station Buran. System integrity 41%. Part of my memory was erased by the frost. I am still... watching the perimeter."}, {"k": ["thanks"], "a": "…don’t mention it. Surviving is the best thanks. The Aether goes quiet when no survivors are left."}, {"k": ["string", "thread", "fern", "sun fern", "progress"], "a": "Warm thread is made from rope with wool or leather. You do not need the desert fern 2,500 blocks away — that was the old recipe. If your recipe still asks for the fern, you are on a pre-R1.2 build: update."}, {"k": ["crowbar", "chest", "locked", "pry", "sealed"], "a": "Locked chests open with a crowbar — crafted from five iron. On builds before R1.2 the config named a crowbar from a mod that is not in the pack, so a fifth of all containers could not be opened at all. Fixed."}, {"k": ["prism", "multimc", "import", "instance", "not supported"], "a": "Prism and MultiMC have their own archive — not the universal one. Take the second button on the download page, then Add Instance → Import → Import from zip. Prism will reject the universal archive."}, {"k": ["map", "minimap", "atlas"], "a": "Checked against the pack files: the map is NOT gated behind quests. It crafts exactly as in vanilla — the pack does not change the recipe. The confusion comes from the quest \"Coordinates in the Ash\" in the First Night chapter: it asks you to bring a map and rewards a compass. So the map is needed for the quest, not the other way round."}, {"k": ["clay", "coke"], "a": "Clay sits under water and ice, but you do not need to get into the water — you will freeze. The overland route: gravel in crushing wheels gives sand, sand under a fan gives clay. Clay gates coke bricks, and those gate steel."}, {"k": ["help", "commands", "what can you do"], "a": "Ask me about: brass, copper, cold, crashes, RAM, shaders, distances, sleep, fire, ice spikes, fuel, string, crowbar, Prism, the map, clay. I remember everything tied to the station."}],
